{"name":"California Roll","hex":"#a09574","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roll","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To revolve by turning over and over; to move by turning on a horizontal axis; to impel forward with a revolving motion on a supporting surface.","To wrap (something) round on itself; to form into a spherical or cylindrical body by causing to turn over and over."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or result of rolling, or state of being rolled.","Something formed into a compact shape by being rolled up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roll"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roger L. Simon","blocks":[{"text":"Roger Lichtenberg Simon is an American novelist and screenwriter. He was formerly CEO of PJ Media and is now its CEO Emeritus. He is the author of eleven novels, including the Moses Wine detective series, seven produced screenplays and two non-fiction books. He has served as president of the West Coast branch of PEN, and as a member of the Board of Directors of the Writers Guild of America; he was also on the faculty of the American Film Institute and the Sundance Institute."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Roger_L_Simon.JPG/330px-Roger_L_Simon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_L._Simon"},{"title":"Osamu Kitajima","blocks":[{"text":"Osamu Kitajima, also known by the pseudonym Justin Heathcliff, is a Japanese musician, producer, composer, and multi-instrumentalist who is known for new-age music, as well as folk, jazz fusion and electronic music."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osamu_Kitajima"},{"title":"California roll","blocks":[{"text":"California roll , or California maki  is a type of sushi that contains imitation crab, avocado, and cucumber. Sometimes crab salad is substituted for the crab stick. In America it comes as uramaki and often the outer layer of rice is sprinkled with toasted sesame seeds or roe. Outside America, California rolls may be closer to the traditional design or futomaki, with nori seaweed on the outside."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/California_Sushi_%2826571101885%29.jpg/330px-California_Sushi_%2826571101885%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_roll"},{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/California_Sushi_mit_Kaviar_%2826545022496%29.jpg/500px-California_Sushi_mit_Kaviar_%2826545022496%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/California_Sushi_mit_Kaviar_%2826545022496%29.jpg/1280px-California_Sushi_mit_Kaviar_%2826545022496%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/California_Sushi_mit_Kaviar_%2826545022496%29.jpg/500px-California_Sushi_mit_Kaviar_%2826545022496%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalifornia_Sushi_mit_Kaviar_(26545022496).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/